design:
Rewrite flickerFactorAt's filter+minByOrNull as a single manual loop tracking the nearest
in-range match, with no intermediate List:

    var nearest: LightEmitter? = null
    var nearestDist = Double.MAX_VALUE
    for ((origin, emitter) in flickerSources) {
        val d = origin.distance(coord)
        if (d <= emitter.radius && d < nearestDist) { nearest = emitter; nearestDist = d }
    }
    return nearest?.flicker?.factorAt(elapsedMs) ?: 1.0

flickerSourcesIn's per-frame re-scan is lower priority -- it's O(emitters) not O(cells), and
"usually a small handful" per its own doc comment. Leave as-is unless profiling says otherwise;
don't over-engineer a cache-invalidation scheme for a cost this small.
